<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>NYT &gt; Technology</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/section/technology</link><description>Technology industry news, commentary, and analysis, with reporting on big tech, startups, and internet culture. The New York Times is a hub for conversation about news and ideas.</description><atom:link rel="self" href="https://rss.nytimes.com/services/xml/rss/nyt/Technology.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>Mistaken Username Sent Man to Prison for 18 Months, Court Finds</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/30/world/canada/wrongful-conviction-kik-username-underscore.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/30/world/canada/wrongful-conviction-kik-username-underscore.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/30/world/canada/wrongful-conviction-kik-username-underscore.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>An appeals court in Canada acquitted Brandon Klayme of charges related to child sexual abuse imagery. His Kik username had one less underscore than another account that was involved.</description><dc:creator>Neil Vigdor</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 30 Jul 2026 09:03:25 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Child pornography</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">False arrest</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Instant messaging</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Kik mobile app</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Decisions and Verdicts</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Dane County</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Halifax Nova Scotia</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/07/29/obituaries/29xp-acquittal-1/29xp-acquittal-1-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Adrian Wyld/The Canadian Press, via ZUMA Press</media:credit><media:description>The Nova Scotia provincial flag. Prosecutors in Nova Scotia acknowledged the conviction had been flawed.</media:description></media:content></item></channel></rss>